CORE
main.c
--enforce-contract foo _ --dfcc main --enforce-contract foo
^EXIT=6$
^SIGNAL=0$
^.*Contract enforcement has already been applied to function 'foo' by a non-DFCC goto-instrument pass.*$
^.*Only one contract may be enforced at a time per function.*$
--
^.*VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL.*$
This test enforces a contract on foo with a plain (non-DFCC) pass, then
enforces the same function under the DFCC pipeline on the resulting
binary. The second invocation must fail: foo is already enforced and the
DFCC pass would re-instrument it. Without the cross-mode guard this case
was silently accepted.
